[I] An event-based networking framework for Internet applications

[T] Twisted is an event-based framework for Internet applications. It includes
[T] a Web server, an SMTP/POP3 server, a telnet server, an SSH server, an
[T] IRC server, a DNS server, a generic client/server pair for remote object
[T] access (Perspective Broker), and APIs for creating new protocols. It
[T] supports integration with GTK+, GTK+ 2, Qt, Tkinter, wxPython, Mac OS X
[T] (PyObjC) and Win32 event loops. It also supports TCP, SSL and TLS, UDP,
[T] Unix sockets, multicast, and serial ports. Supported protocols include
[T] HTTP, FTP, SMTP, POP3, IMAP, TOC, OSCAR (AIM and ICQ), SSH, DNS, IRC,
[T] NNTP, Jabber, SOCKSv4, Telnet, SIP (for VoIP), and XML-RPC and SOAP
[T] using external packages. Most protocols are supported as both servers
[T] and clients.

